Commit:     Viche Executive <executive@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 8 00:02:06 2026 +0000

    Seat registration: validity test, preserve-and-repair, never abort later seats
    
    Draft for Parliament authorisation (handoff H-1794095844-7aa5); not proposed for
    merge. Reported defect: a dangling .git file passed the presence test, so a
    broken seat was silently skipped; a non-empty seat directory without .git hit
    'exit 1', aborting reconciliation for every later seat. Eight of ten live seats
    were broken this way.
    
    Now: a seat counts as registered only if 'git -C <seat> rev-parse --git-dir'
    succeeds. Otherwise the directory is preserved to a timestamped backup, stale
    worktree metadata is pruned, and the seat is re-registered; a failure is logged
    and the loop continues. Structural checks (seat IDs, duplicates, incomplete
    rows) still exit non-zero.
    
    Adds tests/seat-registration-smoke.sh: hermetic minimal town, one seat with a
    dangling .git file and one non-empty seat without .git; asserts both are
    re-registered, the later seat is reached, and both backups retain the seat's
    working file. Passes under /bin/sh and dash.

